    board: file CF-076 — a Tier-2 PASS is bound to a commit that cannot contain the graded change
    
    PERF-013's verdict 88e945ac records passed=true at commit 4720cdc, where
    scripts/project-node.sh, tests/selftest.sh and specs/NODE.md contain 0 occurrences of --layers;
    the fix is the next commit, e21f2ce, with 5 / 7 / 2. The tier-2 detail cites
    "scripts/project-node.sh:54-80 validation", which at 4720cdc is the role/disk-floor block, and
    certifies "selftest user+sys below 1.2 s" while the fix measures 1.54-1.63 s and the board kept
    the row pending as AC-5 unmet.
    
    The same probe prints touches_named_path=0 for CF-055 -> ddff6bc2 (fix bb99a5c) and
    CF-058 -> d15205e (fix 557ac3f), so the misbinding is systemic: the field can carry a commit
    containing the change (CF-054 -> d088bc6, CF-032 -> 8f1e8c1), but nothing requires it.
    
    Filing only — no code, test or spec change. The repair (a verdict-binding audit, a scan_commit
    pointer on every PASS, and a re-judge of PERF-013 at e21f2ce) is the row's acceptance criteria.
    
    Gates at this commit: tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS with 62/62 rows parse;
    scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (18 warnings, all pre-existing classes);
    the board is 62 rows / 62 unique ids with one appended line per file and a byte-identical prefix.
    
    # ch:trace row=CF-076 spec=docs/traceability-doctrine.md wave=none:serial test=tests/selftest.sh::board-rows-parse doc=docs/BOARD.md prompt=prompts/qa.md evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-11-03/88e945ac/verdict.json witness=none:run-dir-untracked-tracked-by-CF-076-AC4 verdict=pending:gitreins-tier2 commit=pending:self-referential
    
